{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Only goodness and mercy shall pursue me</b> — goodness to my soul, and mercy with others, to teach them and instruct them to serve HaShem, until it becomes my fixed habit; for even if I wished to abandon the good for a single moment, it would pursue me." "<b>And I shall dwell</b> — time after time, in the manner of 'the bride runs in their course' (Judges 5:28). Others say: like 'I shall be quiet from distress' (Isaiah 30:15), in the sense of 'in quietness and rest shall you be saved' (Isaiah 30:15). And behold, the meaning is: I shall forever do goodness and mercy; all my days I shall dwell in the house of HaShem, to recognize His deeds — and this is true prayer, for then one separates oneself from other people."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:27.410803654Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}